				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">Is this what we're about?</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3195">Nobbwin</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/20/2001 - 1:43 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2561">Nobbwin</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Nice to see a presence here at guildsay. I've been out of touch a lot, a family illness and death and the Christmas season have conspired to keep me 'awol' for a few weeks now. I hope to be able to put more time into EQ soon in the new year.<br />
<br />
However, I ran across this thread in the Newbie Zone today, and I think it requires an immediate response from the 'ruling council' or whatever the officers are calling themselves these days.<br />
<br />
I dunno if this will link properly:<br />
<br />
http://pub94.ezboard.com/ffirionaviefrm1.showMessage?topicID=933.topic<br />
<br />
I don't want to be a part of any guild that behaves in the way described in that thread. My game style is to roam Norrath helping those in need and having some fun in the process. I can't do that if I&quot;m ashamed to be identified by the tag above my head.<br />
<br />
If I do manage to get on in the next few days, I'll be running ANON until I see either a rebuttal in the thread linked above, or otherwise hear of some action that restores the honour of the Oaken.<br />
<br />
I've enjoyed the few hours I've been able to spend with the Oakies, I've even been able to help some of you. Gotten a few of you killed, too, but I hope I've made amends in those cases. I truly hope that a guild that started out as a pretty decent group of folks isn't devolving into the classic loot farming A-holes that have driven me from other servers.<br />
<br />
Please, Thymbul, Zorx, say it isn't so!						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3195">Nobbwin</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/20/2001 - 2:04 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2561">Nobbwin</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														*sigh* Ok, it's not the Newbie Zone, it's the FV message board. Anyway, we're picking up an extremely bad rep by hogging the ToV camp.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3141">binklewyst</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/20/2001 - 5:05 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2511">Binklewyst</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Hi Nobbwin :)<br />
<br />
It was with great sadness that I read the thread in your link. Basically agree with you. Since I am a warrior I have never been at that site (on FV), and personally know nothing about the incident.  However, I have seen this sort of thing in EQ a lot (been playing almost 2 years).  <br />
<br />
It is amazing the misunderstandings that can occur in this game (even without the language problems), and the bad feelings that follow!  I have personally seen other incidents where it is clear to me that no one is purposely doing anything wrong, but since other people are not seeing the full picture everyone gets upset.  I have no idea if that is what happened here or not, but it would not surprise me.<br />
<br />
In any case, I think it would be worthwhile to work this out with everyone involved.  It's a small server, and Bad Karma will hurt us all!  I do know some (not all) of the people involved, and those people ARE honorable.  In particular, I have seen Annarose perform some highly honorable acts.<br />
<br />
Good luck to ALL involved, whether in OoTO or not!  If I can do anything to help ameliorate the situation, I will.  Unfortunately I will be out of town (and not online) for several weeks, so please forgive me if I do to respond to postings for a while!<br />
<br />
Howbeit; peace to all.<br />
<br />
Binklewyst						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3140">Kimmz</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/20/2001 - 7:03 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2559">Kimmz DenFineste</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2621">Weric</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Now you have to see the point here guys.<br />
On Fiorna Vie there is Trivial loot system, so i dont see it as farming.<br />
You MUST have a lower level to get the page if your over lv22 or so.<br />
I agree that its not good that Shewina fell asleep or something, but it also might have been that she was waiting for help.<br />
She is doing us all a big favour and showing devotion to the guild by staying at this spawn for as long as she did so others can get the ToV.<br />
<br />
And befor that a member of 1st Fist of Light called Rett or something stold Dyllin so i would relly get pissed if somone stole my camp to.<br />
<br />
And as the other person said himself, He thought she was a smuggler, so sorry. i dont buy that he waited long befor he attacked him.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3195">Nobbwin</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/20/2001 - 7:55 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2561">Nobbwin</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Well, this whole thing is nothing but a PR mess. Regardless of how accurate the elf's story is, and I've satisfied myself that it is highly biased, many folks are gonna talk about the Oaken are holding the Starshine camp. I posted a diatribe in our defense based on what I heard tonight in guild chat, but one of the first-hand parties really needs to shut this guy down.<br />
<br />
Here's a link to the page with my blurb:<br />
<br />
http://pub94.ezboard.com/ffirionaviefrm1.showMessageRange?topicID=933.topic&amp;start=21&amp;stop=32<br />
<br />
Might have to cut and paste that, seems URL's aren't parsed on this board.<br />
<br />
In any event, I really think the guild needs to do some damage control in the form of some highly visible public service events. Runningbear volunteered *grin* to organize some, and I'd love to help out. I find that kind of event far more rewarding than farming phat lewt, and would make a real effort to be there.<br />
<br />
-Nobby						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3095">Thymbul</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/21/2001 - 6:02 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2474">Thymbul Thistlefoot</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Okay guys simple as this ... Verrant has no real official camping rules , meaning you get there first its yours . Now in the case of like the orc camp or derv's ect... its one npc per group ect... so no you cant camp a whole camp of orcs for yourself . The problem is the TLC code on the server and the fact it was the ToV , which many people want . Public forums are nothing more then an  Flammer's dream come true . If you want to roam .. then roam  , if you want to camp then camp ... thats my official input . It's not about how others think about us that matters , but how we think about ourselves . Whats been said has been said if theres others that feels the same way as the one thats been offended , oh well ....... If you want to quit the guild because someone had the heart to stick to a camp of a much needed item and in doing so stepped on a few toes , then by all means do . Unfortuantly I've had to camp many items over the years and this is one topic depending on whom's side your on has always been tricky .............						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3195">Nobbwin</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/21/2001 - 7:31 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2561">Nobbwin</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Thymbul, I think you've grossly underestimated the damaging affect of rumor and gossip. On a server as underpopulated as FV, all it takes is one incident, one loud unhappy individual, to negatively affect the gameplay of all of the Oaken. Sure, this particular incident is trivial and will go away, but it exemplifies an attitude that I for one cannot embrace.<br />
<br />
I'm not quitting the guild because Shewina had the 'heart to stick to a camp of a much needed item', I'm quitting the guild because it's leadership lacks the heart to respond to someone with a grievance against it. The guild's honour has been damaged, and I don't intend to have my own honour damaged by association.<br />
<br />
I've not had an opportunity to contribute much to the guild, and by the same token I haven't benefitted much myself from membership. So I doubt I will be missed, and we can part amicably. Good luck and safe journeys to you all.<br />
<br />
--Nobbwin						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3166">dt17464</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/21/2001 - 7:41 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2568">Vytek</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2569">Ridale</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														It took me over 4 weeks to get my ToV.  That guy is a cry baby.  He had to run out and post on Public Boards to try and trash our guild.  From what I understand, he got his page last night.  He has yet to mention that the Guild let him get the next Pop.<br />
<br />
If our guild was not there, some other would be.  When I was tring to get my ToV. There were other guilds farming it.  I had to wait a long time.  Did I run out and Flame them on message boards because they were being unfair and scream like a baby?  He got his page in 2 or 3 days after flaming us,  What a baby.<br />
<br />
Nobbiw I have not had the pleasure of grouping with you yet,  and I thank you for what you said on that thread to defend our interests there and would hate to see you leave our guild.   I have played with several other players from other guilds my level and have lots of friends not in the Oaken.  I don't want my reputation tarnished by the actions of my fellow guild mates as well.  <br />
<br />
In this paticular issue,  I side with my guildmates and I am not ashamed of there actions.   TLC Does not get do anything to prevent Camping.  Folks are just going to be more creative in getting the Rare items that we all love to have.<br />
<br />
<br />
vytek and Ridale<br />
<br />
P.S.  I never read that board before today and have been playing EQ since its been out.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3053">Bobmato</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/21/2001 - 1:09 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2479">Bobmato Zek</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I have been trying to post a response to the issue in the FVMB but I get an error every time.<br />
<br />
Thymbul I have to strongly disagree with you.  It does very much matter how our FV community views us.  We can not simple say forget what they think, as long as we feel good about ourselves.  We are not the only guild on the server and we will in time have to deal with others.  A bad reputation will make that difficult at best.<br />
<br />
I am not informed on the exact events, only having the posts to go by, but if the monk form our order (Shewina?) could not take the mob on her own, why was she the only one there?  We can’t sit on a very popular camp by parking someone there permanently and calling to others when Dyllin pops.  That just isn't ethical or honorable.  If we get the item needed, leave the camp for someone else.  <br />
<br />
Note that this individual is not content, but plans to continue to attack our reputation with a sit-in at the Dyllin sapwn loc.<br />
<br />
http://pub94.ezboard.com/ffirionaviefrm4.showMessage?topicID=185.topic<br />
<br />
Nobbwin--Sorry to see you go.						</td>
					</tr>
